' Use case diagram for section 2 (2-use-case-diagram.md), part 3 of 3: slaughter and sales.
' The farm's use case diagram is split into three figures by stage of the batch
' (use-case-rearing, use-case-procurement, use-case-slaughter-sales); all use the identical boundary label.
' Ovals with a section 3 table carry its number (UC-01..UC-04) for traceability.
' Rendered with Graphviz dot. Re-render after editing:
'   java -jar tools/plantuml.jar -tpng diagrams/use-case-slaughter-sales.puml   (needs Graphviz 'dot')
' Layout: actors on the left except the Trusted Representative (`RW -- TR`, `SMBA -- TR`, on the right).
' No Worker here: who slaughters client orders in-house is not in the sources, so only the Director and Client are linked.
' Client (small 50-100-bird orders, section 0) is its own actor, not a kind of Buyer, so the Buyer subtypes do not inherit Slaughter Client Order.
' Buyers on the right put
'   the Buyer -> Sell Meat line beside the generalisation triangle, which reads ambiguously; the cost is the Bazaar
'   Agent line crossing the title. An include from Sell Meat to Bazaar Agent to Arrange Delivery scatters the layout,
'   so UC-04 step 2 describes the driver without naming Arrange Delivery.
@startuml
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 14

actor "Director" as DIR
actor "Slaughter Crew" as CREW
actor "Client" as CL
actor "Buyer" as BUY
actor "Bazaar Agent" as BA
actor "Nurata Seller" as NS
actor "Shop Customer" as SHC
actor "Trusted Representative" as TR
rectangle "Nurota Halol Parranda: current operations" {
  usecase "UC-02\nDecide Main Slaughter Date" as DS
  usecase "Weigh Sample Birds" as WS
  usecase "UC-03\nRun Main Slaughter" as MS
  usecase "Pay Slaughter Crew" as PC
  usecase "Slaughter Client Order" as SC
  usecase "Arrange Delivery" as AD
  usecase "Sell Meat" as SM
  usecase "UC-04\nSell Meat to Bazaar Agent" as SMBA
  usecase "Agree Price per kg" as AP
  usecase "Send Weight Photo by Telegram" as WP
  usecase "Record Bazaar Weighings" as RW
  usecase "Record in pDaftar" as PD
}
DIR -- DS
DIR -- MS
DIR -- PC
DIR -- SC
DIR -- AD
DIR -- SM
DS ..> WS : <<include>>
PC ..> PD : <<include>>
AD ..> PD : <<include>>
SM ..> PD : <<include>>
SM <|-- SMBA
SMBA ..> AP : <<include>>
SMBA ..> WP : <<include>>
SMBA ..> RW : <<include>>
CREW -- DS
CREW -- MS
CREW -- PC
CL -- SC
BUY -- SM
BA -- SMBA
BA -- WP
RW -- TR
SMBA -- TR
BUY <|-- BA
BUY <|-- NS
BUY <|-- SHC
@enduml
